From: LilSmokeOS developers
Subject: [PATCH] libretro: keep the no-GL stub independent of GL types

The stub only needs the state enum. glsm.h includes GL/gl.h even in a
software-only build. No graphics implementation is added by this change.

--- a/libretro/libretro.c
+++ b/libretro/libretro.c
@@ -74,6 +74,6 @@
  * rglgen pulls in on iOS are ES ones that do not carry them. glsm.h alone is
  * enough here - the stub needs the enum and nothing else. */
-#include <glsm/glsm.h>
+#include <glsm/glsm_state_ctl.h>
 bool glsm_ctl(enum glsm_state_ctl state, void *data) { return false; }
 #endif
 
